  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "References and public procurement",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Manage > Manage and monitor",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN applies to all central government departments including their executive agencies and non-departmental public bodies (collectively referred to as 'in-scope organisations').",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The PPN sets out recommended policy to accept requests for references, especially if the supplier has performed well and / or has exceeded expectations. References should normally be in support of a specific contract and in-scope organisations should avoid providing \"open\" references (i.e. a general statement about a supplier not related to any specific contract).",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "There is no legal impediment to providing references but any opinions offered must be backed by records. For example if commenting on supplier performance, such evidence might include the achievement (or not) of delivery milestones or performance against key performance indicators (KPIs). Subjective assessments should be avoided.",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Recommended policy is to accept requests for references in connection with the performance of a specific public contract.",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In-scope organisations should:",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "in accordance with recommended policy, accept requests for references, especially if the supplier has performed well and / or exceeded expectations",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "establish whether requests for references are made pursuant to the policy on taking account of bidders’ past performance as set out in PPN 04/15; and where the case, comply with the procedures regarding certificates of performance",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that opinions offered in relation to reference requests are backed by contemporaneous records",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "avoid providing \"open\" references and instead provide references in support of a specific contract",
      "ordinal": 13,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00014",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure only staff formally authorised to speak on behalf of the in-scope organisation provide references. References should normally be given in writing and recorded internally.",
      "ordinal": 14,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00015",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 15,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00016",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This PPN should be read alongside the relevant parts of the legal framework but it is not designed to provide guidance on a particular clause or regulation from the Public Contracts Regulations 2015 (PCR 2015).",
      "ordinal": 16,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00017",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Additional support and guidance",
      "ordinal": 17,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00018",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Make sure you:",
      "ordinal": 18,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00019",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "read the PPN and any supporting implementation guidance",
      "ordinal": 19,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00020",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "seek legal and commercial advice in the context of specific procurements",
      "ordinal": 20,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Additional support and guidance"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00021",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "This applies to",
      "ordinal": 21,
      "heading_path": [
        "References and public procurement",
        "Additional support and guidance",
        "This applies to"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
